// Self-contained runtime shim for the site-asset manifest, the Term (`@term/site`) analog of the React
// the React site-asset accessor build-time accessor. Provided to Seed via <global:asset> (docked
// `name asset`, so this object IS the binding); the `.tree` accessor (../asset.tree) calls `asset/get` /
// `asset/try-get` / `asset/entry`. A namespace object (not top-level functions) so the bundled client has no
// name collisions, matching the resize / fontset / title runtimes.
//
// Why the manifest is EMBEDDED here rather than `import`ed from ./assets.json (as the React asset.ts does):
// the production Cloudflare cast concatenates this shim's raw source as a prelude in front of the compiled app
// (see deck/make.tree native prelude), so a relative `import` would not resolve from the bundle's location. The
// manifest is inlined instead. This is the ONLY difference from asset.ts; the API + behavior (throw-vs-null,
// the manifest shape) are identical. assets.json stays the canonical data file that sync change-detects against;
// this snapshot is regenerated from it on every sync.
